# Virtualenvs -- rebuild from requirements.lock.txt / requirements-gen.lock.txt
.venv/
.venv-gen/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generator model weights (9.5 GB). Re-fetch by pinned revision + sha256 from
# generators/DOWNLOAD_RECORD.json; the EMA slim export is described in
# generators/spring_f5/checkpoints/EMA_EXTRACTION.json.
generators/**/*.safetensors
generators/**/*.pt
generators/**/*.onnx
generators/**/*.bin
generators/*/f5_tts/
generators/*/.cache/
generators/*/README.md

# Audio. 46,078 wav files, ~6.5 GB. Every manifest carries a per-clip sha256, and the
# SPRING_F5 clips carry their generation seed, so the audio is reproducible from the
# manifests that ARE tracked here. See docs/MIGRATION.md.
data/*/audio/

# Source corpora as downloaded (OpenSLR wav, IndicVoices parquet, MMS). The small
# line-index transcripts under data/openslr_raw are kept, the audio is not.
data/openslr_raw/*/
data/mms_raw/
data/indicvoices_raw/*/

# Vendored ASVspoof 2021 baseline weights (70.5 MB) -- see weights/PROVENANCE.md for
# the source URL and checksum.
weights/*.pth

# Scratch
*.tmp
_tmp_*.txt

# --- overrides for the repo-root .gitignore ---
# VoiceShield-AI's top-level .gitignore excludes *.pth/*.pt/*.onnx/*.wav globally, which
# is right for the app but would drop the trained detectors. These twelve checkpoints are
# the irreplaceable output of the experiment series -- training has GPU nondeterminism, so
# unlike the audio they cannot be regenerated bit-for-bit. 71 MB each, inside GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit. Audio stays excluded.
# Only the five checkpoints the documentation actually cites are tracked: the frozen
# v0.1, the v1 safe baseline, f5-trimmed (best unseen-spoof), iv15 (best all-round) and
# asdg-bal (best FLEURS). The seven historical checkpoints stay local -- their training
# curves are kept as history.json, which is what the write-ups reference.
!checkpoints_v1/best_model.pth
!checkpoints_f5_trimmed/best_model.pth
!checkpoints_f5_iv15/best_model.pth
!checkpoints_asdg_bal/best_model.pth
!frozen/*.pth

# SSL research: downloaded checkpoints (1.2 GB) -- pinned in
# models/spectra_aasist/DOWNLOAD_RECORD.json with sha256
models/
